# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .dockerignore
#
# Excludes files and directories from the Docker build context.
# A tight .dockerignore is essential for fast builds:
#   - Without it, node_modules (~400MB) and .next (~1GB) are sent to the
#     Docker daemon on every `docker build`, even if they're not needed.
#   - With it, only source files (~5MB) are sent, making builds 10x faster.
#
# Rule: include the minimum needed to build the app.
# Everything not explicitly needed by a COPY instruction can be excluded.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Dependencies (will be reinstalled inside Docker) ─────────────────────────
**/node_modules/
**/.npm/

# ── Build outputs (will be rebuilt inside Docker) ────────────────────────────
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/out/
**/.turbo/

# ── Environment files (injected via docker-compose.yml, never baked in) ──────
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/.env.development
**/.env.production

# ── Version control ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore

# ── Editor and OS artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Test artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/coverage/
**/__snapshots__/

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# ── Docker files themselves ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Excluded to prevent accidental context pollution; Docker already has them.
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
.dockerignore

# ── Documentation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
README.md
docs/
